 worry about it you're fine  language is not about performing for a  grade for a mark for a test  language is about communicating so if  your communication needs are largely to  understand things then you should be  working very hard on increasing your  passive vocabulary and it's also easier  to increase your passive vocabulary by  continuing to read and listen  and you know increasing your  understanding your grip on these words  until they will slowly slide into  the active ledger but there will always  be a much smaller number of them  furthermore  we will always make mistakes we will  always struggle for words  in a foreign language  why do people expect that they're going  to perform somehow perfectly in a  foreign language you aren't going to  so i say passive vocabulary is great the  more of it you have the greater the  potential for you to convert some of  those passive words into active words  and  uh the different things that you can do  like reviewing them in flashcards to  become more attentive  that all helps  obviously talking helps to be able to  use them you've got to use them  i i'm not a great fan of correcting  people when they speak and that's why at  least when we have our online  conversations we try not to correct  while people are speaking but we type  out all the words and phrases that they  misuse  and we send them a report which they  then can study so you have the time at  your leisure to study these and slowly  slowly and you will also as with  everything in language you'll just be  able to use certain words at times then  you'll forget certain words at times so  again don't expect perfection when  you're working on a second language but  passive vocabulary is great and it'll  gradually convert itself into active  vocabulary  as you as you use them  so i guess that was uh that was the main  thing on this uh what was the other one  they said  um yeah so i don't believe that you have  to use a word in order to remember it  but you do have to use it in order for  it to be active if you haven't used it  it's not active  uh but you can build up the potential  for active  vocabulary by continuing to expand your  passive vocabulary  there we go  thank you very much i hope this makes  sense
 

